      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:5:21:2",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الْأَعْمَى تَجُوزُ شَهَادَتُهُ قَالَ نَعَمْ إِذَا أَثْبَتَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Al Hajjal, from Sa’albat Bin Maymoun, from Muhammad Bin Qays who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about the blind, is his testimony allowed?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Yes, when it is proved’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from al-Hajjal from Tha‘labah ibn Maymun from Muhammad ibn Qays who has narrated the following: “I once asked abu Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the testimony of a blind man if it is admissible. He (the Imam) said, ‘Yes, it is admissible if he has preserved it.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
